 "sentences": [
  "To that end, I want you to keep the following in mind: always start your method names with 'x_'.",
  "This is a convention we follow to easily identify custom methods within our codebases.",
  "Well-placed comments can greatly enhance the understandability of your code for your colleagues and future maintainers.",
  "So, please remember to add comments wherever necessary.",
  "I trust that you'll keep these practices in mind as you work on your projects.",
  "Don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or concerns.",
  "Feel free to stop by my desk if you need anything at all.",
  "They can sometimes impose unnecessary restrictions and distract from our specific style guidelines.",
  "Secondly, we have a specific convention for naming methods and functions.",
  "I want you to always start method names with 'md_' and function names with a single 'd_'.",
  "This is to maintain consistency across our codebases and make it easier to identify and distinguish between the two.",
  "That's it for now.",
  "I just wanted to clarify these points as they are important for maintaining our code quality and readability.",
  "That's precisely it.",
  "By reducing the need to switch between windows, you can stay focused and immersed in your work.",
  "It's all about creating a seamless and efficient workflow.",
  "Don't hesitate to provide any feedback on how this setup improves your productivity."
 ],
